  "observations": [
    "Actual south frontage is a six-storey off-white residential elevation with simple narrow pale-frame windows and two timber glazed entrances.",
    "Low mottled stone plinth, upright drainpipes and stacks of pale metal-railed balconies at both ends are visible. Balcony artwork remains on the original LoD2 plane; no real balcony geometry is added.",
    "Nine exact rendered/HCOL street probes show a 2.4–2.6m slope. Upper windows and floor bands stay horizontal at the qualified high-street datum; the low stone plinth and each fixed-height timber entrance follow the local measured floor.",
    "Six residential rows fill the literal source eave height: the northern block has taller row spacing than the opposite Kalliolanrinne4 front. The end balcony stacks follow the same five upper row heights.",
    "Each timber entrance retains its individually authored2.6–2.8m height at its local native street floor; it is not stretched to the high end of the whole street. Upper residential window rows remain level."
  ],
